The 3D view is drawn with three.js (MIT). Its grid, dimensions and prompting
at a spot follow ideas from QuiCAD by the QuiCAD authors (Apache-2.0).
The agents' build123d quick reference (src/agent/quickref.js) is adapted from
CAD Khana's references/build123d_quickref.md by the CAD Khana authors
(Apache-2.0), modified to refer to Duckbench's tools. The fit and printability
checks (python/runner.py) follow CAD Khana's approach.
Geometry conversion uses ocp-tessellate by Bernhard Walter (Apache-2.0).
CAD modeling uses build123d by the build123d Contributors (Apache-2.0).
The editor uses Monaco Editor by Microsoft (MIT).
Browser CAD execution uses Pyodide and OCP.wasm by Yeicor and contributors.

The About page contains upstream license texts and attribution notices,
including build123d's NOTICE. Generated copies are also shipped in licenses/.
